PATCH 478: the M3 Bradley weapon-station step 899c and its four station handlers (8121/8176/81bb/8205) --
the exact twins of the AH-64 pair fixed in patch 474, reached a few thousand frames later in the same
AZER1 self-play.

899c (asm 0x899c-0x89ed) dispatches `lcall word[CS:0x89ee + station*2]`, a FAR-pointer table of four
0f69: entries (0x8a91/0x8ae6/0x8b2b/0x8b75 = FUN_1000_8121/8176/81bb/8205); Ghidra deref'd that CS table
as a host pointer and made the call near, so the first M3 that reached a firing state SEGV'd.  Each
handler is the patch-429/462 idiom (`dec rounds; a265 aim; b1df(type) -> SI=the NEW projectile, DI=the
firer; launch wrapper; reload; c047 report`), with station 0 additionally reporting the TOW launch against
a vehicle target via bfeb and station 6 (the cannon) rate-gated on (word[0x6cde]&7)==0.
